  "title": "UMTS RLC: Make Coverity happy about initializing members",
  "description": "Comment out a rlc_seq struct member that isn't used. Initialize\na struct member before copying it to a pointer instead of intializing\nit in the pointer afterwards. (This is dumb and inferior, though\npossibly will be optimized away, but Coverity complains about\ninitializing *seq_new with an uinitialized member that is immediately\noverwritten otherwise.) Reorder the struct members to put the nstime_t\nfirst and group the 32 and 16 bit items together, which is marginally\nbetter on platforms with 8 bit alignment.\n\nCoverity CID 1499435",
